   ok: portal.css has no colour literal: every colour is a token

## 2. Journey 1: Ana, a member, signs in with OpenID Connect (26-sso)
   concept: authorization code flow with PKCE: the portal keeps state, nonce and the code verifier server-side, sends only the S256 challenge, swaps the code for tokens on the back channel, and maps the IdP's groups to a portal role
   axe / (signed out)                         0 violations
   GET http://127.0.0.1:53159/auth ? redirect_uri, scope, state, nonce, code_challenge, code_challenge_method, client_id, response_type
     code_challenge_method=S256, code_challenge=4cOrjSbYNSfZ..., scope=openid email profile portal
   ok: the browser is sent to the IdP with a PKCE S256 challenge, a state and a nonce, and no secret
   axe IdP sign-in page                       0 violations
   back at /dashboard; cookie sid: HttpOnly=true, SameSite=Lax; users row: {"sub":"ana","role":"member","org_id":"acme","member_id":"M0001"}
   ok: signed in as a member of Acme (group portal-members, member_no M0001), in an HttpOnly session cookie
   ok: the session table holds the cookie's sha256, never the cookie
   ok: the login transaction was consumed by the callback

## 3. The dashboard: a server-rendered page (20-portal) over RLS (37-authorization), formatted with Intl (25-bilingual)
   concept: the page is an async server component; its query runs as the `app` role with Ana's identity set for the transaction, so RLS filters it too; amounts go through Intl.NumberFormat, months through Intl.DateTimeFormat
   Hello Ana | 6 months | total €2,343.75 (SQL: 2343.75) | first row: September 2026 €162.50 €243.75 €406.25
   ok: six months of contributions, and the total is the database's sum, formatted en-GB
   axe /dashboard (en)                        0 violations
   as app role with Ana's identity, no WHERE clause: contributions 6 of 144, members 1 of 24, events 0 of 69
   ok: RLS alone limits a member to her own rows, even for a query without a WHERE clause

